  "worked_solution": "We perform the multiplication under a single radical and then simplify the result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3z}\\cdot \\sqrt{5{z}^{6}} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{3z\\cdot 5{z}^{6}} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{{z}^{6}\\cdot 15z} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{{({z}^{3})}^{2}\\cdot 15z} & = \\\\ \\sqrt{{({z}^{3})}^{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{15z} & = \\\\ |{z}^{3}|\\cdot \\sqrt{15z} & = \\\\ |z{|}^{3}\\cdot \\sqrt{15z} & =\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $z\\ge 0,$ we have $|z|=z,$ and we can simplify further. Therefore, our final answer is\n\n$$\n|z{|}^{3}\\cdot \\sqrt{15z}={z}^{3}\\sqrt{15z}.\n$$",
